    {
      "id": "p0136-b008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Daihinmin (\"Great Pauper\"), more commonly known as Daifugo (\"Great Millionaire\"), is similar to the card games known as \"Tycoon\" and \"President\" in English. The goal of the game is to get rid of all your cards as quickly as possible. The winner of each round is declared the daifugo and the loser is called the daihinmin, so it's somewhat funny to imagine this goofy dog being both things at the same time.",
        "raw": "Daihinmin (\"Great Pauper\"), more commonly known as Daifugo (\"Great\nMillionaire\"), is similar to the card games known as \"Tycoon\" and \"President\"\nin English. The goal of the game is to get rid of all your cards as quickly as\npossible. The winner of each round is declared the daifugo and the loser is\ncalled the daihinmin, so it's somewhat funny to imagine this goofy dog being\nboth things at the same time.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29458394,
          0.79228571,
          0.89541398,
          0.89642143
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28994153,
          0.79157143,
          0.90092365,
          0.89749286
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          38,
          39,
          40,
          41,
          42,
          43
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "Daihinmin 的意思是“大贫民”，不过更常用的名称是“大富豪”（Daifugō），类似英语中的 Tycoon 或 President。玩家要尽快打光手中的牌，赢家成为“大富豪”，输家成为“大贫民”。于是，独自玩牌的狗既是大富豪，又是大贫民，笑点便保留了下来。",
